Title: Frontmatter migration: one type field, one shape, across the corpus
Created: 2026-09-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-10T15:50Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Ranking reads frontmatter, and the frontmatter is not uniform enough to rank
on. Across roughly 954 bodies: 47 carry no frontmatter type at all, 208 use a
top-level `type:`, and 746 use `metadata.type`. Until that converges, any
per-type or score-carrying field is reading two schemas and a gap.

This ticket is **only** the migration. The grammar, the resolver, `supersedes`
and the scorer are `0914`; they were bundled here and the bundle was three
units.

Design reference: defect 3 in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`. Review: sizing in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design-review-fable-design.md` §3.

## Relevant files

- `projects/*/memory/*.md` and `memory/*.md` — the corpus
- `skills/memory/SKILL.md` — the shape new memories are written in

## Actions

1. Converge on one shape and one field name.
2. Migrate the 208 top-level and type the 47 untyped. A data change of this
   size is reviewable by count and by spot-check, not by reading 954 diffs —
   say so in the pull request and give the counts.
3. Update the skill so new memories are written in the surviving shape.

## Test

A lint test with a **deliberately untyped fixture**, so the check fails on a
real case rather than passing because the corpus happens to be clean. "47
untyped are now typed" is a count-of-zero and passes vacuously the day after.

## Verification

- [ ] Counts before and after, stated in the pull request
- [ ] The lint fixture fails without the fix and passes with it
- [ ] A spot-check sample of migrated bodies reads correctly

## Invariants

- No body content changes. This is a frontmatter migration.
- No body is deleted.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One shape, one field name, across the whole corpus
- [ ] The skill writes the surviving shape
- [ ] A lint test with an untyped fixture guards the convergence
